    """Develop a comprehensive guide to CUDA stream callbacks and their applications in scheduling, asynchronous work, and CPU-GPU synchronization. Start by explaining stream callbacks: functions executed on the host CPU when all previously launched operations on a stream complete. Discuss how callbacks provide asynchronous notification without GPU-CPU synchronization overhead of explicit CPU-GPU barriers. Explain applications: scheduling dependent operations that can't be expressed as GPU kernels, checking results without blocking, and coordinating multi-GPU workloads. Discuss the semantics: callback execution occurs at the driver level, not necessarily on the main thread, and careful handling is needed. Cover how to use callbacks for dynamic kernels: launching new work based on GPU computation results without waiting for the GPU. Explain how callbacks integrate with other synchronization mechanisms: events, explicit synchronization. Discuss limitations: callbacks can't directly affect GPU operations already queued, so careful sequencing is necessary. Include practical examples: using callbacks to implement conditional kernel launches, adaptive batch sizing based on intermediate results, and asynchronous result collection. Cover debugging and profiling: understanding when callbacks execute relative to GPU operations. Discuss how callbacks interact with multiple streams and their ordering guarantees. Finally, explain best practices: keeping callbacks lightweight, avoiding unnecessary CPU-GPU synchronization, and structured use of callbacks versus explicit event-based synchronization.""",

